== Structure

This work starts by showing and discussing the fundamental, psychological backgrounds for the term emotion and which features are necessary to identify them. Further the classifcation approaches in machine and deep learning are presented showing their unsupervised and supervised methods for training and feature extraction. At the end of Chapter 2 the datasets for the further implementation parts are introduced. Related works are presented to display current research on multi-modal detection and their different methods and learning proceedings. Continuing with the design and implementation of the different supervised models, Chapter 4 presents self-trained and also pretrained models and how to expand as well as finetune their knowledge. In addition the architectures to fuse the information for multi-model emotion detection are shown and different fusion methods are discussed including some kinds of basic scoring and more advanced feature combinations. These accomplishments are evaluated in Chapter 5 introducting measurement criterias for relieable and comparable results. At the end this thesis is summarized and gives an overwiev in comparison to some outcomes from related work concluding with a look on possible future work in emotion detection.


